<title>PORTUGAL: Yield 5.50 on Portuguese three-month bills.</title>
<headline>Yield 5.50 on Portuguese three-month bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield eased to 5.500 percent, from 5.716 percent previously, at the Institute for Public Credit Management's sale of 91-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Institute placed 9.5 billion escudos of the 15 billion on offer.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
